# Rust FFI Core

`Lux.Rust.FFI` defines the Elixir side of the checked-in Rust FFI crate at
`priv/rust/lux_ffi`.

The Rust crate exports two C ABI symbols:

```text
lux_ffi_execute_json(*const u8, usize) -> LuxFfiBuffer
lux_ffi_free_buffer(LuxFfiBuffer)
```

`lux_ffi_execute_json` accepts UTF-8 JSON bytes shaped as:

```json
{"operation": "type_of", "input": "lux"}
```

and returns an owned response buffer containing:

```json
{"ok": true, "value": {"type": "string"}}
```

Elixir callers can build and inspect the payload contract without loading a
native library at compile time:

```elixir
alias Lux.Rust.FFI

{:ok, request} = FFI.request(:sum_i64, [1, 2, 3])
FFI.abi()
FFI.safety_contract()
FFI.cargo_commands()
```

The response buffer is owned by the caller and must be released exactly once with
`lux_ffi_free_buffer`.
